      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "The complete Shantonagh Lodge holding. A three-bedroom home, separate two-bedroom guest lodge and circa 36.7 acres, offered together as Lot 1.\r\n\r\nHouse. Guest lodge. Land. All in one holding.\r\n\r\nThere is a lot to this property.\r\n\r\nAt its heart is a three-bedroom, three-bathroom home where the money was spent on the things that matter. Behind it sits a fully self-contained two-bedroom guest lodge. Around them are mature grounds, traditional outbuildings and two substantial blocks of agricultural land.\r\n\r\nTogether, they form a holding that works on several levels.\r\n\r\nThe Main Home\r\n\r\nThe house has character, but the quality behind it is what stands out.\r\n\r\nHigh ceilings and large sash windows bring natural light through the accommodation. Original fireplaces, decorative cornices and panelled doors remain, alongside handmade solid teak, double-glazed sash windows with traditional internal shutters.\r\n\r\nThe living accommodation is well balanced. There is room to gather and room to get away from it, with separate reception areas and a contemporary kitchen and dining space at the centre of everyday life.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen is finished with high-quality fitted cabinetry, generous worktop space, a Rangemaster cooker and Belfast sink. White goods are included in the sale.\r\n\r\nThere is oil-fired central heating, with underfloor heating at ground-floor level and radiators upstairs. Fibre broadband is also available.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, there is no drop-off in standard. High ceilings continue through the first floor, alongside three bedrooms, three bathrooms overall and carefully chosen finishes.\r\n\r\nThe main bathroom is particularly well done, with a freestanding roll-top bath, separate enclosed shower and double vanity with twin basins.\r\n\r\nTraditional detail. Modern comfort. And a standard of finish that runs right through the house.\r\n\r\nThe Guest Lodge\r\n\r\nBehind the main home is a separate two-bedroom, one-bathroom guest lodge.\r\n\r\nAnd this is a proper home in its own right.\r\n\r\nAt its centre is a long open living and dining area with a high vaulted ceiling, exposed timber roof trusses and extensive glazing bringing natural light through the room. A freestanding solid-fuel stove provides a natural focal point.\r\n\r\nAlongside is a full-size contemporary kitchen with fitted cabinetry, generous worktop space and its own Rangemaster cooker.\r\n\r\nFor extended family, visiting guests or as a potential additional income stream, the lodge gives the holding another level of flexibility.\r\n\r\nThe Grounds\r\n\r\nThe house and guest lodge sit within mature, established grounds.\r\n\r\nTrees and planting provide privacy around the buildings, while a sheltered courtyard creates a separate outdoor space close to the house.\r\n\r\nTo the south is a further green area with established apple trees, an old hay shed and traditional stone outbuildings previously used for agricultural purposes.\r\n\r\nThese older buildings form another useful part of the holding and provide further possibilities for future use.\r\n\r\nThe Land\r\n\r\nBeyond the house and guest lodge, the complete holding extends to circa 36.7 acres.\r\n\r\nThe lands are arranged in two principal blocks.\r\n\r\nApproximately 23.55 acres lie predominantly behind the main property. The lands are divided into a number of natural fields by established hedgerows and benefit from extensive public road frontage and direct access.\r\n\r\nThis section also includes a triangular parcel across the public road with further road frontage and potential for a residential site, subject to the necessary planning permission.\r\n\r\nA further circa 12.17 acres lie directly across the public road from Shantonagh Lodge.\r\n\r\nThis is a compact block with direct road access, good frontage and established field boundaries. A number of traditional stone outbuildings are also situated on this section of the holding and may provide further potential, subject to any necessary planning consents.\r\n\r\nA quality home. Independent guest accommodation. Mature grounds. Outbuildings. Agricultural land. Road frontage.\r\nAll offered together.\r\n\r\nLocation\r\n\r\nShantonagh Lodge is approximately 13 km from Castleblayney, 13 km from Carrickmacross and 23 km from Kingscourt, providing straightforward access to shops, schools, services and everyday amenities across all three towns.\r\n\r\nFour Buying Options\r\n\r\nWhile Lot 1 represents the complete Shantonagh Lodge holding, the property is also being offered in three individual lots:\r\n\r\nLot 1: The complete holding, including the home, guest lodge and circa 36.7 acres\r\nLot 2: The 3 bedroom home and 2 bedroom guest lodge on circa 1 acre\r\nLot 3: Circa 23.55 acres of agricultural land\r\nLot 4: Circa 12.17 acres of agricultural land\r\n\r\nBuyers interested in any of the individual lots can view the separate listings or contact Keenan Auctioneers for full details and maps.\r\nFor further information or to arrange a viewing, contact Keenan Auctioneers on 042 966 7224.\r\n\r\nKey Features\r\n•\tComplete holding extending to circa 36.7 acres\r\n•\t3 bedroom, 3 bathroom main home\r\n•\tSeparate 2 bedroom, 1 bathroom guest lodge\r\n•\tHigh standard of finish throughout\r\n•\tHandmade solid teak double-glazed sash windows\r\n•\tTraditional panelled internal shutters\r\n•\tHigh ceilings and original architectural details\r\n•\tContemporary kitchen with Rangemaster cooker and Belfast sink\r\n•\tOil-fired central heating with underfloor heating at ground-floor level\r\n•\tGuest lodge with vaulted ceiling and exposed timber trusses\r\n•\tFull-size guest lodge kitchen with Rangemaster cooker\r\n•\tMature gardens and sheltered courtyard\r\n•\tOld hay shed and traditional stone outbuildings\r\n•\tCirca 23.55-acre land parcel with extensive public road frontage\r\n•\tCirca 12.17-acre land parcel with direct public road access\r\n•\tFibre broadband available\r\n•\tCirca 13 km from Castleblayney and Carrickmacross\r\n•\tOffered as the complete holding or through three individual lots\r\n\r\nExplore Shantonagh Lodge\r\n\r\nTake a closer look inside both the main home and guest lodge with our interactive virtual tours.\r\n\r\nMain Home Virtual Tour:\r\nhttps://my.matterport.com/show/?m=EKjPXUqRbQ1\r\n\r\nGuest Lodge Virtual Tour:\r\nhttps://my.matterport.com/show/?m=B5SdRbBVvGL"
      },
